{"content":"1|//! Per-task root-password elevation at MutationEngine's dispatch choke point.
2|//!
3|//! A protected call (the `elevation` plugin's policy) needs, besides the
4|//! caller's verified session and exact grant, a one-time ticket issued by
5|//! `elevation.authorize_task` for that exact call: same principal, session,
6|//! plugin, method and canonical arguments. Issuing a ticket checks the
7|//! root password through PAM service `op-dbus-elevate`. There is no
8|//! principal-to-Unix-account map. The authenticated caller remains the
9|//! principal; checking the password never switches it to root. Tickets live
10|//! in memory, are single-use and expire after
11|//! `TICKET_TTL_SECONDS`; a bridge restart drops them. Repeated failures lock
12|//! the principal out for a while. The password is never stored or logged,
13|//! and `authorize_task` arguments are redacted from the chain record.
14|//!
15|//! The check sits behind [`SudoAuthority`] so a polkit-backed authority can
16|//! replace the PAM one without touching the protected methods.
17|
18|use std::{
19|    collections::HashMap,
20|    sync::{Arc, Mutex, OnceLock},
21|};
22|
23|use anyhow::{Context, Result, bail, ensure};
24|use chrono::{DateTime, Duration, Utc};
25|use op_plugins::state_plugins::{
26|    elevation::{
27|        AUTHORIZE_CAPABILITY, AuthorizeTaskInput, AuthorizeTaskOutput, ListProtectedActionsOutput,
28|        TICKET_TTL_SECONDS, protected_action, protected_actions, validate_authorize_input,
29|    },
30|    json_render::gallery::canonical_json,
31|};
32|use serde_json::Value;
33|use sha2::{Digest, Sha256};
34|
35|use crate::{
36|    interceptor::load_capability_grants, mutation_engine::MutationEngine, project_dispatch,
37|};
38|
39|pub(crate) const PAM_SERVICE: &str = "op-dbus-elevate";
40|const TICKET_DOMAIN: &str = "opdbus.elevation.ticket.v1";
41|const MAX_FAILURES: u32 = 5;
42|const LOCKOUT_MINUTES: i64 = 15;
43|const MAX_TICKETS_PER_PRINCIPAL: usize = 16;
44|
45|/// Checks a password against the fixed elevation account, not the caller.
46|pub(crate) trait SudoAuthority: Send + Sync {
47|    fn verify(&self, user: &str, password: &str) -> Result<bool>;
48|}
49|
50|/// Production authority: PAM verifies the root password and account validity.
51|pub(crate) struct PamSudoAuthority;
52|
53|impl SudoAuthority for PamSudoAuthority {
54|    fn verify(&self, user: &str, password: &str) -> Result<bool> {
55|        ensure!(user == "root", "elevation checks only the root password");
56|        crate::pam_auth::check_password(PAM_SERVICE, user, password)
57|    }
